# Secrets — REQ-N3, CLAUDE.md rule 9. Never commit a real .env.
# Ignore every .env variant, then allow back only the committed templates,
# which contain no values. A denylist of specific names misses the next one
# somebody creates — and .env.test already held a real SESSION_SECRET.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test.example

# Research working documents. Untracked at the owner's request, 2026-09-10.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE RELYING ON IT. These files are no longer versioned or backed
# up by git, and they are the thesis. Two consequences were accepted knowingly:
#
#  1. analysis-plan.md is a pre-registration document — it is written before the
#     data exists, and its value depends on being able to show WHEN. The commit
#     date was that evidence. There is now no record of it in this repository,
#     so if an examiner asks whether the analysis was chosen before or after the
#     results were seen, the repository cannot answer.
#  2. docs/03-research/experiments/TEMPLATE.md goes with them, so a fresh clone
#     has no experiment template and the new-experiment procedure in
#     .claude/skills/ has nothing to copy from.
#
# Keep a backup somewhere that is not this laptop.
docs/03-research/
docs/00-archived/hypotheses-2026-08.md

# Local uploads. Product photos go to object storage in deployment (D-3);
